on/math-academy-id "q-66600" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=1,$ then what is $3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-4\\pi )-4?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-2$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=1,$ then $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-4\\pi )=1.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-4\\pi )-4=3(1)-4=3-4=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-66600/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce45704e-ecea-5c67-bb40-a413f8a0d72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66600"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fa23b878-4512-5961-8a9b-7ec2b3faa47f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "ce774c87-b728-54bd-b827-3ffd493a5c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer/id #uuid "46cc1c2b-bbd7-5077-8f29-9d43e17c1972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "ef939884-e6ab-54f0-aa19-02f9ad88f86a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "366b466d-acc9-5fd4-b0c7-7de567eea0b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "22dfa9ec-7d90-56a7-a1f6-d817a92ea5ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70612/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer-field/choices ["q-70612/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-70612/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-70612/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" "q-70612/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-70612/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70612" :question/id #uuid "d979fe3c-7ab1-5ad7-af8f-289e038a869f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70612" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ then what is $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+6\\pi )?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=3$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+2\\cdot 3\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+6\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ then $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x+6\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70612/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce45704e-ecea-5c67-bb40-a413f8a0d72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-136551"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13942972/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nNotice that our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. If we reflect the graph about the $y$-axis, we get the same picture. This means that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡a \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "42e4db29-12d2-5d31-8e0e-049e6f59d03d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "277e420e-a5db-580c-a84e-f42ec3b56ace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049/selection/1af1be23805790c46357e9fb162ca653a9aaa7ac9fc36768624c7a181010a146" :answer/id #uuid "00ae29a7-0dbc-564c-a947-56886602f7d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "1e87649b-6131-5a33-8f89-55e576475a20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049/selection/d1a8a37ee79915a85d677d2ddaece5fbc32c08d998af71a8574eaecf24bbb21e" :answer/id #uuid "60bfb2ab-2037-5210-ad84-5459557acec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f16938f3-027a-5145-8bbb-97644bb31c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158049/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer-field/choices ["q-158049/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" "q-158049/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" "q-158049/selection/1af1be23805790c46357e9fb162ca653a9aaa7ac9fc36768624c7a181010a146" "q-158049/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-158049/selection/d1a8a37ee79915a85d677d2ddaece5fbc32c08d998af71a8574eaecf24bbb21e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158049" :question/id #uuid "f9d793a4-ed3e-56ac-92ce-7b4313dd241b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158049" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{sec}⁡a=\\sqrt{7},$ then $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+20\\pi )=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13942972/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. This means that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+20\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+2\\pi \\cdot 10) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡a \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-a+20\\pi )=\\sqrt{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-158049/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b378b0-30e5-59a8-b9f7-882b5e226a2e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053/selection/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" :answer/id #uuid "9303f81f-7136-5912-b034-83c0fca9f7a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6ca619f5-7e84-5d4a-8e7d-7b06470e55ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "6a603595-0c84-58b9-b9bd-0b530b000af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "9c81b46f-0f52-5627-95c5-4dc4f1aaf40a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "a5ea223c-3f32-5ed4-87b4-03709db6577b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "82541927-f188-55f4-8090-684b0e41d14d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158053/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-158053/selection/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" "q-158053/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-158053/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-158053/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-158053/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158053" :question/id #uuid "a8817eeb-ad4b-51b9-be15-71e5a745e14f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158053" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{3},$ then $6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+8\\pi )+7=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13942972/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. This means that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+8\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-x+8\\pi )+7 & =6(-\\frac{5}{3})+7 \\\\  & =-10+7 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-158053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b378b0-30e5-59a8-b9f7-882b5e226a2e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
